From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nydal91 <nydal91@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:48:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Capture the Vulkan window when the surface comes from
 vkGetInstanceProcAddr

Under Wine the game gets vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR past the detoured vulkan-1
export, so the menu started with a null window and never received input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A9WqnwGsLAcGJXd49N2pes
---
 OptiScaler/hooks/Vulkan_Hooks.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/OptiScaler/hooks/Vulkan_Hooks.cpp b/OptiScaler/hooks/Vulkan_Hooks.cpp
index 902e4fe..224ada8 100644
--- a/OptiScaler/hooks/Vulkan_Hooks.cpp
+++ b/OptiScaler/hooks/Vulkan_Hooks.cpp
@@ -1390,6 +1390,14 @@ PFN_vkVoidFunction hkvkGetInstanceProcAddr(VkInstance instance, const char* pNam
     {
         return (PFN_vkVoidFunction) hkvkDestroyDevice;
     }
+    else if (procName == std::string("vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR"))
+    {
+        // Wine resolves this past the vulkan-1 export, the menu gets no window for its input without it
+        if (o_vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR == nullptr)
+            o_vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR = (PFN_vkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR) orgFunc;
+
+        return (PFN_vkVoidFunction) hkvkCreateWin32SurfaceKHR;
+    }
 
     if (auto direct = StreamlineSwapchainFunction(pName, _ReturnAddress()))
         return direct;
